Article 93
(1) Every employer who employs Women is obligated to maintain:
   a. dignity;
      honor;
      decency;
      safety; and security.
(2) The obligations of Employers to Women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by Employers while female workers are at the workplace and during working hours that have been determined.
(3) Working hours as referred to in paragraph (2) apply to Women who enter into employment agreements for a definite period as well as for an indefinite period.
(4) Fixed-term employment agreements entered into by Employers and female workers must be made in writing and must use the Indonesian language and Latin script.
(5) Fixed-term employment agreements made by Employers and female workers may only be made for certain work which according to the type and nature or activity of the work will be completed within a certain time, namely as follows:
   a. Work that is completed once or is temporary in nature;
   b. Work that is estimated to be completed within a not too long period of time;
   c. Work that is seasonal in nature;
   d. Work related to new products, new activities, or additional products that are still in trial or exploration; or
   e. Work whose type and nature or activity is not permanent.
(6) Fixed-term employment agreements made by Employers and female workers cannot be entered into for work that is permanent in nature.
(7) Fixed-term employment agreements that do not meet the provisions as referred to in paragraph (5) and paragraph (6) shall by law become indefinite-term employment agreements.

