d. assistance related to parents' difficulties in handling educational bureaucracy for Children.

Article 21
In order to realize the objective of improving the quality of life of Women and families as referred to in Article 20 letter [letter not specified in source text], it is carried out through:
a. providing access for Women to enjoy education services, health services, and other strategic fields;
b. encouraging the involvement of Women in the development process;
c. providing knowledge, skills, character values, morals, and family resilience;
d. encouraging programs that can increase the independence of Women in the economic, political, legal, social, cultural fields, as well as other strategic fields; and
e. providing opportunities and chances to every Woman to occupy various positions and posts in various fields of work, including strategic positions, as long as it is in accordance with her capacity and capability.

Article 165
Strengthening and development of institutions providing services for improving the quality of life of Children as referred to in Article 163 letter are carried out through:
a. increasing the resource capacity of institutions providing services for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region;
b. assistance in implementing services for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region;
c. development of materials and implementation of Communication, Information, and Education for the fulfillment of Children's rights for institutions providing services for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region;
d. strengthening networks among institutions providing services for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region;
e. facilitation of the implementation of standardization of institutions providing services for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region; and
f. development of institutions providing services for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region.

Article 35
Capacity building for Women in the economic sector as referred to in Article 34 letter is carried out by means of:
a. increasing training programs for Women business actors;
b. making maximum efforts so that Women in the Region obtain access to capital through financial institutions;
c. preparing an alternative capital system for Women micro-economic actors in the Region;
d. developing alternative fund/facility support for Women innovators; and
e. providing and assisting in providing market access for MSME products produced by Women in the Region.

Article 185
Provision of services for Children requiring special protection as referred to in Article 166 letter ... is carried out through:
a. implementation of the provision of services for Children requiring special protection through the Regional Apparatus that administers Government Affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the Region;
b. provision of public complaint services for Children requiring special protection in the Region;
c. provision of outreach services for Children requiring special protection in the Region;
d. provision of case management services for Children requiring special protection in the Region;
e. provision of temporary shelter services for Children requiring special protection in the Region;
f. provision of mediation services for Children requiring special protection in the Region;
g. provision of assistance services for Children requiring special protection in the Region; and
h. provision of service facilities and infrastructure for Children requiring special protection in the Region.

Article 186
Strengthening and development of service provider institutions for Children requiring special protection as referred to in Article 166 letter (huruf) [unspecified] is carried out through:
a. increasing the capacity of the resources of service provider institutions providing protection and handling for Children requiring special protection in the Region;
b. providing specific needs for Children in special situations and conditions in the Region;
c. providing communication, information, and education on the protection of Children requiring special protection in the Region;
d. strengthening networks among service provider institutions providing protection for Children requiring special protection in the Region; and
e. facilitating the implementation of standardization of service provider institutions providing protection for Children requiring special protection in the Region.

Article 66
